Subject: vulkan: let GGML_VK_DISABLE_HOST_VISIBLE_VIDMEM reach UMA devices

Same edit and rationale as vulkan-uma-honor-disable-host-visible-vidmem-b11541.patch
(PR #22930 / commit 32120c10e3 makes the device->uma branch of
ggml_vk_create_buffer_device() request a host-visible type first, so on an AMD
APU under the Windows proprietary driver the weights land in pageable shared
memory instead of the BIOS-carved dedicated heap, and
GGML_VK_DISABLE_HOST_VISIBLE_VIDMEM is unreachable on UMA). This patch makes the
variable work on UMA: when set, prefer the dedicated heap and keep the
host-visible options as fallbacks. No default changes.

Regenerated against the Unsloth source tarball
llama.cpp-source-b12651-mix-c7059d6.tar.gz (upstream b12651 plus Unsloth pins),
where the non-UMA branch below the edit became
`else if (!device->rebar || device->disable_host_visible_vidmem)`, which broke
the b11541 patch's context. The edit itself is unchanged.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp
@@ -224,11 +224,21 @@
             buf = ggml_vk_create_buffer(device, size, {vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent,
                                                        vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal});
         } else if (device->uma) {
-            // On UMA, prefer host-visible memory so direct tensor borrowing works.
-            // If unavailable, fall back to device-local memory.
-            buf = ggml_vk_create_buffer(device, size, {vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent,
-                                                       vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal,
-                                                       vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent});
+            if (device->disable_host_visible_vidmem) {
+                // Carve-first: on an APU with a BIOS-reserved (dedicated) heap, a
+                // host-visible type can shadow it and push the weights into pageable
+                // shared memory. Ask for the dedicated heap first, keep the rest as
+                // fallbacks.
+                buf = ggml_vk_create_buffer(device, size, {vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal,
+                                                           vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent,
+                                                           vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent});
+            } else {
+                // On UMA, prefer host-visible memory so direct tensor borrowing works.
+                // If unavailable, fall back to device-local memory.
+                buf = ggml_vk_create_buffer(device, size, {vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent,
+                                                           vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal,
+                                                           vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible | vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostCoherent});
+            }
         } else if (!device->rebar || device->disable_host_visible_vidmem) {
             if (device->allow_sysmem_fallback) {
                 buf = ggml_vk_create_buffer(device, size, {vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal,
